## Summary

I extracted **17 program graphs** from the Current Finance (Pebble Protocol) Sui Move lending protocol specification. The specification was fetched from the Sherlock audit contest README at `https://github.com/NyxFoundation/audit-current/blob/main/README.md`, and source code was read from the local clone at `/Users/hiro/Documents/2026-03-currentsui-contest-march-2026-grandchildrice-main/sui-move-contract/`.

### Functional Units Identified

The program graphs cover the complete lifecycle of the lending protocol:

**Core Lending Operations (SG-001 through SG-005):**
- **enter_market** -- Obligation creation with emode group binding
- **deposit** -- Collateral deposit with ctoken minting via exchange rate
- **withdraw** -- Collateral withdrawal with obligation safety check
- **borrow** -- Asset borrowing with multi-level limit enforcement (min borrow, emode group cap, global cap, obligation safety)
- **repay** -- Debt repayment with partial/full repay paths and refund handling

**Liquidation (SG-006, SG-012, SG-013):**
- **liquidation** -- Normal soft liquidation with close_factor limiting
- **auto_deleverage_borrow** -- ADL for excess borrow situations with time-decaying LTV threshold
- **auto_deleverage_collateral** -- ADL for excess collateral deposits

**Protocol Mechanics (SG-007 through SG-011):**
- **flash_loan** -- Hot potato pattern flash loan with per-emode fee rates
- **interest_accrual** -- Three-segment piecewise linear interest rate model with borrow index
- **exchange_rate** -- ctoken minting/burning via exchange rate calculation
- **obligation_safety** -- Weighted debt vs adjusted collateral risk check
- **emode_management** -- E-mode group creation and per-asset parameter configuration

**Infrastructure (SG-014 through SG-017):**
- **reserve_lifecycle** -- Reserve cash/debt/supply state machine
- **obligation_debt** -- Per-CoinType debt tracking with collateral conflict prevention
- **oracle_price_feed** -- Pyth oracle integration with EMA/spot divergence checks
- **claim_reward** -- Liquidity mining reward claiming

All `.mmd` files are written to `/Users/hiro/Documents/security-agent/outputs/graphs/batch_w0b0_1773060675/current-finance/` and include YAML frontmatter titles, `stateDiagram-v2` syntax, and `note right of` blocks encoding key invariants (82 total invariants across all graphs).

